            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for suggestion!\r\n\r\nNot having a customizable config in fixed table structure is intentional. Mostly because it would need to have complicated rules in order to achieve the flexibility of a current single function approach.\r\n\r\nYour question about how to customize per filetype confirms this argument. I would suggest doing something like this:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal blocked_filetypes = { ['neo-tree'] = true }\r\n\r\nrequire(\"mini.statusline\").setup({\r\n\tcontent = {\r\n\t\tactive = function()\r\n\t\t\t-- Customize statusline content for blocked filetypes to your liking\r\n\t\t\tif blocked_filetypes[vim.bo.filetype] then return '' end\r\n\t\t\t-- Continue the function\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe way you add git blame section seems good to me (as long as `git_blame` is always a string).\r\n\r\nClosing as the function approach probably won't change.",
